This program demonstrates the use of the Semi-Consistent Method (SCM) for simulating deformable soil in a physics simulation environment using the Chrono Engine. The simulation involves a rigid body interacting with a deformable terrain, where the terrain's behavior is modeled using the SCM semi-empirical model. The program uses the Irrlicht library for visualization and the Chrono Vehicle module for terrain modeling.

