This Python script processes financial data from multiple sources to calculate Market-On-Market (MOM) ratios. It reads daily market capitalization (market cap) data from Excel files and closing prices from text files, both provided by different financial data providers. The script then calculates various metrics such as past-year returns, splits the data into different market segments based on market cap and momentum, and finally computes the MOM ratio for each segment.

