### Overview

This Python script is designed to automate the process of downloading GeoIP databases from MaxMind, verifying their integrity using SHA-256 checksums, and uploading them to an Amazon S3 bucket. It is intended to be run as a Lambda function within AWS CloudFormation, handling both creation and update events.

### Global Variables and Standalone Functions

#### Global Variables
- `s3bucket_name`: The name of the S3 bucket where the GeoIP databases will be stored.
- `license_key`: The license key required to access the GeoIP database downloads.
- `s3key_prefix`: The prefix under which files will be stored in the S3 bucket (default is `'GeoLite2/'`).

#### Standalone Functions
- `download_file(filename)`: Downloads the specified GeoIP database file from MaxMind and saves it locally.
- `put_to_s3(filename)`: Uploads the downloaded GeoIP database file to the specified S3 bucket after verifying its integrity.
- `send(event, context, responseStatus, responseData, physicalResourceId=None, noEcho=False)`: Sends a response back to CloudFormation indicating the success or failure of the operation.
- `lambda_handler(event, context)`: The main entry point for the Lambda function
*************
