### Overview

This Python module provides XML encoders for various types of parameters used in Web Processing Service (WPS) version 1.0. It includes functions to encode process descriptions, execution responses, and output definitions. The module leverages classes from the `eoxserver.services.ows.wps.parameters` and `eoxserver.services.ows.wps.v10.util` modules to represent different types of parameters and their attributes.

### Classes and Structs

#### `LiteralData`, `ComplexData`, `BoundingBoxData`

These classes represent different types of parameters that can be processed in a WPS service. They inherit from a base class and define properties such as identifier, title, abstract, and more.

#### `AllowedAny`, `AllowedEnum`, `AllowedRange`, `AllowedRangeCollection`, `AllowedByReference`

These classes define the constraints on the values that a parameter can accept. For example, `AllowedEnum` specifies a set of allowed values, while `AllowedRange` defines a numeric range.

