# Comprehensive Natural Language Documentation for `QuadCFInterp`

## Overview
The `QuadCFInterp` class provides functionality for performing quadratic coarse-fine interpolation in computational fluid dynamics simulations. It handles both scalar and vector fields, ensuring accurate boundary conditions across different levels of refinement.

## Classes and Structs

### Class: `QuadCFInterp`
This class is the main class responsible for performing the interpolation operations. It contains several member variables and methods to manage the interpolation process.

#### Fields
- **`newCFInterMode`:** A boolean flag indicating whether to use the new "moving window" version of the CF stencil building algorithm.
- **`m_isDefined`:** A boolean flag indicating whether the object has been properly defined.
- **`m_level`:** An integer representing the current level of refinement.
- **`m_dxFine`:** A real number representing the fine grid spacing.
- **`m_refRatio`:** An integer representing the refinement ratio between levels.
- **`m_nComp`:** An integer representing the number of components in the field.
- **`m_domainFine`:** A `ProblemDomain` object representing the domain of the fine grid.
- **`m_inputFineLayout`:** A `DisjointBoxLayout
